{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "c2d045c4-9174-8e97-800f-b8cd35398161",
  "created_at": "2026-02-11T12:05:23-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Kathleen Kearney",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:00:42-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:00:46-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good afternoon. This is Kathleen Kearney, I'm out on Harrison Avenue, and I've got a storm drain in front of my house that's just not doing its job. Again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:00:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Mrs. Kearney, I'm sorry to hear that. What's the house number on Harrison?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:01:06-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "358. Fort Adams side, you go down past the turn and we're on the left. Been here a lot of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:01:16-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "358 Harrison Avenue. Got it. And tell me what the drain is doing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:01:22-05:00",
      "duration": 25,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's grunting. That's the only word I've got for it. You can hear it gurgling and then it's slow, so slow, and any time we get a thaw, the snow melts off, it backs right up into the street. And it's not even raining. No storm, nothing. It's a dry day today and there's water sitting there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:01:47-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So this is without any storm, just melt or even just a regular day?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:01:54-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Melt, mostly. The sun comes out, the banks go soft, and the drain can't take it. Today it's bad enough that the water's running down toward my neighbor's garage. He's got the door at the low end of his driveway. I'm out there looking at it, I'm watching it creep."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:02:16-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Toward the neighbor's garage. Is it up to the door yet, or still in the driveway?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:02:24-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Still in the driveway, about halfway, I'd say. But it's moving. I'm pacing around the kitchen here, I switched to one of those standing desks and I can't sit still anyway, so I keep going to the window."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:02:41-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Let me write that down. Water backing up from the drain in front of 358 Harrison, no storm, and it's heading to the neighbor's garage. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:02:54-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Now let me ask you something, because I've been told two different things. Is that a city drain or a state one? Somebody at the church said Harrison is a state road down there and somebody else said no, it's the city's."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:03:13-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a fair question. Harrison Avenue is a city street as far as I know, and the drains on it would normally be ours. If it turns out that one belongs to the state, we'd be the ones to pass it along, so you don't have to chase it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:03:34-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Because I'm tired of the runaround. This isn't the first time I've noticed it, it does the same thing every thaw and nobody has cleared it out that I can see."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:03:48-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. I'll put it in as a drain that backs up repeatedly in dry weather, and I'll mark it as water heading toward a neighboring property, so it gets looked at sooner rather than later."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:04-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd appreciate that. Somebody should come with whatever the truck is, the vacuum thing, and clear it out. Probably leaves and sand in there from the fall, and now ice."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:17-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could well be it. Is the drain right at the curb in front of your house, or a little up or down the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:28-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right at the curb, directly in front. You can't miss it, it's the one with the puddle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:36-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Okay. And do you want a call back when the crew has been out, or would you rather just watch for them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:47-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Call me back, yes. It's 401-555-0197."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:50-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0197. Let me read that back to be sure. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-seven."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:56-05:00",
      "duration": 1,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:04:57-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I've got it all down. Someone from the drainage crew should get to it in the next few days, and if it gets worse, if the water actually reaches that garage, call us right back and we'll bump it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:05:15-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I will. I'm not shy about it. Thank you, Lorraine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:05:20-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mrs. Kearney. Take care."
    }
  ],
